      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-03-04_WidnesExaminer_art0001" n="art0001">
        <p>IN AID OF LOCAL WAR FUNDS. WARRINGTON MUSICAL SOCIETY.</p>
        <p>GRAND CONCERT, 'PARR HALL, WEDNESDAY, MARCH 15th. MISCELLANEOUS PROGRAMME, including Sir Filarles V. Stanford's "Last Post," H. J. Taylor's ' The Eve of Waterloo," and Sir Edward Elgar's :Carillon," the poem in which will be recited by xilis Lucy Nutiall. ARTISTES: Miss LUCY NUTTALL, Vocalist; Mde, MARGUERITE STILWELL, Solo Piano- . Mr. ALFRED ROSS, Solo Violin.</p>
        <p>CHORUS AND ORCHESTRA. Conductor: Mr. FRANK H. CROSSLEY. ()Deb at 7 D.in. Commence at 7.30. Carriages at 10. Ticket-holders admitted at 6.46. ADM/SSION (Reserved), 3/-, 2/-, 116, (Unreserved) _ . .</p>
        <p>r_LAN- OPEN MONDAY NEXT, March Gth, at Pearson's, 'Bridge-street. Unreserved tickets at I'eurson's and Dawson's, Sanker.street.</p>
        <p>LIONEL Ft.kIRCLOI7GH, Hon. Sec.</p>
      </div>
