        <p>_ At the Borough Police Court 'on liondai-, Joseph 11.41 brook, traffic;ins-peetor on the L. and N.-W. Railway, was ' granted temporart autho'fity. to 'Sell at the Off-liCence, 'sB,.Leghi 'street, in place of. MTS. Elizabeth Watkin.s. . , .</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-03-04_WidnesExaminer_art0111" n="art0111">
        <head>Latchford Garden _Society.</head>
        <p>Latchford Garden _Society.</p>
        <p>The annual meeting of .the Latchfora Garden Society is to be held on Wednesdkv evening next, at 7.30 p.m.,- in the Wash-lane School- room. Those interested in the work are re- questkl to attend, as several important matters are due for discussion.. - '</p>
        <p>British Women's Temperance Association.</p>
        <p>The monthly meeting was held on Wednes- day afternoon in .Bold-street Church Parlour_ The President (Sirs. Owen) presided. A vote of sympathy with the, late secretary, Mrs. Simpson, in her recent bereavement was</p>
