      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-03-04_WidnesExaminer_art0215" n="art0215">
        <head>SALES BY AUCTION SALES BY AUCTION By Messrs. A. H. CLIVE &amp; Co.</head>
        <p>SALES BY AUCTION SALES BY AUCTION By Messrs. A. H. CLIVE &amp; Co.</p>
        <p>TAYLOR, CHALMERS &amp; CO.,</p>
        <p>AI7CTIONEEIS AND VALUERS, ESTATE AND INSURANCE ' AGENTS, 15, BOLD-STREET, WARRINGTON. Sales by Auction, Valuations for Probate, Sale, or Mortgage, Rents Collected. Tel. No. 228.</p>
        <p>TO MANUFACTURERS, WAREHOUSEMEN AND 'INVESTORS. FREEHOLD PROPERTY AT WARRINGTON. .To Close :the Trust of the late William Hunt. TO BE SOLD BY AUCTION by MESSRS. A. H. CLIVE &amp; CO., at the Blue Bell Inn, Horsemarket-street, Warrington, on Wednes- day, the 15th day of March, 1916, at five o'clock in the afternoon, subject to the Public Sale Conditions of the Incorporated Law Society of Liverpool, and to such Special Conditions as shall be then and there read. Lot I.—All that Modern Freehold DWELL- ING-HOUSE, situate and being No.. 37, Lythgoes-lane, Warrington; in the occupation of Mr. James Hunt. Together with the site thereof. Gross annual .rental A:l4 19s, landlord paying rates. The house contains large kitchen, larder, large parlour, and scullery on ground floor; 2 • large bedrooms, bathroom and W.c. 11. and c.</p>
        <p>water throughout. 34 feet frontage (double), and would command a higher rental. • • Lot 2.—A1l those Three Freehold COTTAGES,' Nos. 39„ 41, and 43, Lvthgoes-lane, Warrington, in the occupation of Ilmsrs. Jones, Hunt. and Gallop. Together with the site thereof. Gross annual rental ,t3O us., landlord paving rates. And also all that large plot of VACANT LAND lying behind Nos. 39, 41 and 43, containing altogether about 500 square yards, with cart en- trance from Lythgoes-lane. suitable for the erection of a Manufactory, Warehouse or Work- shop. Lots 1 and 2 will first he offered for Sale together, the total site contents being 694 k square yards. - For. further particulars and to see plan apply to the Auctioneers at their offices, 6, Egypt- street, Warrington; or to 11. J. LONGTON, Solicitor, King-street, Warrington.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-03-04_WidnesExaminer_art0216" n="art0216">
        <head>By Mr. ROBERT LOWE.</head>
        <p>By Mr. ROBERT LOWE.</p>
        <p>PENKETH. Removed for Convenience of Sale to</p>
        <p>THE RED LION INN. WARRINGTON-ROAD</p>
        <p>PENXETII. SATURDAY NEXT, MARCH urn, at 2 o'clock. MRR. ROBERT LOWE will SELL BY , AUCTION a Superior lot of Household , FURNITURE and other Effects, removed from the Belgian Home, at Hall Nook, Penketh, and other goods, mostly the manufacture of Messrs. Robert Garnett and Sons, and Messrs. Sankey, consisting of: Excellent Carved Mahogany Bed room Suite, Mahogany Bedstead; Spring Mat- tresses, Wool Bed and Bedding. Set Brass and Iron Bedsteads, Cloth Rug. Fenders, Fire Irons, Steel Stool, Dining Table, Mahogany Dumb Waiter. Couch and four Chairs, two Pairs Bronzes (horses and gladiators), Carving Chair, Pictures, large ,Meat Sale Crockery, Pans, Side Table, Bath, &amp;c., Oak Roll-top Desk, Revolving Chair. Dinner Waggon, two Chests Drawers, two Oak Umbrella Stands, Washstand, Dressing Table and Pedestal, several odd Chairs, Dinner Gong. Oak Stand, two Oblong Tables, six Mir- rors, Hand Bell, and other effects. _ _</p>
        <p>Mo.st of the above are almost new. Terms cash. On view morning of Sale</p>
        <p>PRELIMINARY ADVERTISEMENT. MARKET GATE SALE ROOMS, WARRINGTON.</p>
        <p>Re Estate of the late WILLIAM BINGERM, Wire- drawer, Great Sankey, deceased, removed for convenience of sale. WEDNESDAY. MARCH 15. at 2 o'clock. SALE BY AUCTION of the Superior House- hold FURNITURE and Antique Effects. Catalogues on application. • ROBERT Lows, Auctioneer.</p>
        <p>By Messrs. JOHN MAINWARING &amp; Co.</p>
        <p>51, WILSON-PATTEN-STREET, WARRINQTON. MO BE SOLD BY AUCTION by MESSRS. JOHN MAIN WARING &amp; CO., at the Blue Bell Inn, Horsemarket-street, Warrington, on Wednesday, the 15th day of March. 1916; at Five o'clock in the Evening prompt, subject to the Public Sale Conditions of the Liverpool Law Society and to other conditions to be then produced; All that Desirable DWELLING-HOUSE, No. 52, Wilson-Patten-street, Warrington, recently in the occupation of the late Mrs. Daniel Jones, containing Entrance Hall, • Dining Room, Drawing Room, Kitchen, Pantry, Scullery and Cellar; six Bedrooms, two ,Boxrooms, Bathroom and W.c.,. and the usual Out offices. The house is well furnished with blinds, cup- boards, gas fittings, cornice poles, and good fire-places. The property is well built and in a good state of repair, and in part has been recently decorated.</p>
        <p>Vacant possession will be given. The Tenure is Leasehold for a term of 999 years from the 25th March, 1877, and is sold subject to an apportioned yearly ground rent of .C 5 16s. 6d.</p>
        <p>For further particulars and to view, apply to the Auctioneers, at their Offices in Bridge-street, Warrington; or to</p>
        <p>.TnomAs RIDGWAY, Solicitor, 2, Cairo-street, Warrington.</p>
        <p>Domestic Servants.</p>
        <p>BETWEEN (.111{L Wanted for doetoria house, aged 16 or 17; cook and housemaid kept.- 41trily Aire. Lowe, Home Lea, Boothstown, near Itanchester.</p>
        <p>fIOOK-GENERAL (good) Wanted immedi- Li ately for Ashton-on-Morsey; plain cooking; all duties; two in family; good references required.— Write Box 17, " Examiner " Office, Warrington. ,COOK-GENERAL (experienced) Wanted, or Working Housekeeper, and Housemaid- aitresa; doctor's house; family 2; no washing: near Macclesfield.—Write Box D., " Examiner '; Office, Warrington. COOK-GENERAL Wanted immediately, refer- ences essential.—Apply 10, Hanover Gardens, ' Broughton Park, Manchester.</p>
        <p>COOK-GENERAI2 Wanted; must be reliable; good wages paid.—Apply " Westleigh." Maul- deth-road, Heaton Mersey. Manchester.</p>
        <p>COOK-GENERAL (good) Wanted; three in family; Housemaid-Waitress kept.—Apply, stating wages, references, to 'Mrs, Porritt, Beech- field, Bamford, Rochdale.</p>
        <p>_ FOR SOUTHPORT.—Good GENERAL, able to wash and cook; and GIRL, about 16, to assist in housework.—Apply first by letter, to Mrs. R. H. Gee, 60, Rawlinson-road, Southport. GENERAL (experienced) Wanted at once.— Mrs. Bullough, " Sttndiield," Hall-lane, Hind- ley, near Wigan.</p>
        <p>- - GENERAL Wanted for elderly lady; Sefton Park; no family; £26; small house, light and homely situation.—Phillips, 133, Smithdown-road, Liverpool (Domestic Servants' Registry),</p>
        <p>GENERAL (good) Wanted at once; references required.-718, Greasby-road, laiscard, Wal- lasey.</p>
        <p>GENERAL (experienced) Wanted; Protest- ant; good plain cooking; no washing; small family; daily help given.—After 7.30„ or write, 32, Birch-road, Oxton, .13irkenhead.</p>
        <p>GENERAL MAID Wanted immediately, age 19 to 24; wages £l4. Also Wardmaid, at end of March; wages Xl4.—Mornings, Matron. St. Paul's _Eye Hospital, Oldhall-street,_Liverpool. GENERAL-Wanted immediately for doctor's house; comfortable home; light work: family three; £l6; fare paid; liberal outings; references.- 1 Wellington-street, Littleborough, Lancashire. GENERAL (experienced) Wanted; two in family; good wages; references.—Mrs. Mudd, Carlton Villa, Park-road, Hindley, Wigan.</p>
        <p>GENERAL Wanted, good cook, age 20 to 30-; small family ; good wages and home.—Harri- son, 1, Winstet Avenue, West Didsbury, Manches- ter.</p>
        <p>GENERAL (superior) Wanted, able to cook; family two; references required.—Grant, Glenavon, Cavendish Drive, Rock Ferry.</p>
        <p>GENERAL (young, 22-24) Wanted, to assist in house and shop; good wages to reliable girl; references.—Address Mrs. Bond, 8, St: James'-street, Southport.</p>
        <p>GENERAL (good) Wanted; references re- quired.—Mrs. Hewitt,. 22, Woodlands-road, Cheetham Hill. Manchester. GENERAL (experienced) Wanted; housemaid kept; good wages.-12, Mersey-avenue, Aig- burth. Liverpoel.</p>
        <p>- - - GENERAL (smart) Wanted, age 18 to 20; comfortable home for energetic girl; three in family.—Write J. Webb, 64, Plungington-road, Preston, Lancashire.</p>
        <p>GENERAL (good) Wanted, for small family; no children.—Apply 34, Wellington-road, Whalley Range, Manchester. GENERAL (young) Wanted, 18 to 20; 3 in family; no cooking.-56, Parsonage-road, Withington.</p>
        <p>GENERAL SERVANT (good) Wanted; help given; liberal wages.—Apply Mrs. Schofield. West Bank, Healey, Rochdale. GIRL (smart) Wanted, as Useful Help for all duties; wages to commence 8/- per week, ris- ing to 12/-.—Mrs. Lomas, Florist, Prestwich, near Manchester.</p>
        <p>GIRL (smart) Wanted for housework and assist in the bar.—Apply Volunteer Hotel, Sale.</p>
        <p>GML,.about 16, Wanted, to mind baby; live in; reference required.-18, Crosby-road, Waterloo, Liverpool.</p>
        <p>UL -Wanted to assist in house, age 14 to 16; lur no children; mod home.—Apply 672, Chester road (corner of Warwick-road), Old Trafford, Man- chester.</p>
        <p>110USE-PARLOURMAID Wanted; Protest- ant; experienced.—Apply, stating age, wages required, 12, Warren Drive, Now Brighton.</p>
        <p>II- - OUSE -PARLOURMAID Wanted; small family; four maids kept; good references re- quired.,--Apply Miss Macgregor, Hillcarr, Altrinc- ham.</p>
        <p>HOUSEMAID-WAITRESS and Betweenmaid Wanted; Protestants • good workers; family four; wages £l9, £16.--Letters, Taylor, "New- stead," Wavertree. - -</p>
        <p>li[EAD LAUNDRESS Wanted, salary ..E:30; 4th and 6th Laundresses, 16 and .£ 17 ; Head Ritchenmaid, £2O; materisi.• for dresses.--Apply Matron, Royal Infirmary, Oldham.</p>
        <p>- _ HOUSEMAID Wanted; fond of children; good wages.-12, Mersey-avenue, Aigburth, Liverpool.</p>
        <p>V.A NT S of all classes Wanted at once; )...7 places waiting.—Sterland's, Yew-street, Brough- ton, Manchester, S 0 IJ THPORT. —GENERAL Wanted, age 16: 18; two in family.-30, Walmer-road, Birkdale, Southport.</p>
        <p>MWO GENERALS Wanted, used to kitchen work.—Royal Yacht Hotel, Duke-street, Liver- pool. TTSEFITL HELP.—Wanted Young Girl; perience not necessary • comfortable home.— Apply Mrs. Leech, Sterndale. Cheadle, Cheshire. _ _ WORKING HOI7SEICF;EPER or GENE-RAT Wanted; 3 in family.—By letter, stating wages. to Mrs. Colenso, Rathmoylon, Gorsehill-road, New Brighton.</p>
        <p>:VOIJNG GIRL Wanted, end of April, to learn • cooking: small family; 2 maids: references required; coed wages to suitable eirl.—Mrs. Higgin- botham, Fallibroome, Macclesfield.</p>
      </div>
