        <p>WARRINGTON UNION. TENDERS. Persons willing to contract for the';supply of any of the undermentiened articlo, to be delivered free .of expense at the Workhouse, Warrington, or Cottage Homes, Padgate, at such times, and in Such quantities, as the Guardians or their offiCers may require, are requested to send in Tenders to me not later than '5 p.m. on; Tuesday, • the 21st March, 1916, and the same. will be considered by the Guardians nt a ineet- ing to be held on Wednesday, the 22nd March, 1916. From Ist April. 1916, to 31st March, 1.917, Milk—Workhouse and Cottage Homes. • Uniforms for' Male Officers. - From Ist April, 1914,. to 30th September, 1016, *Crockery Groceries &amp; Necessaries Coal and Slack. ~. Thirds Boots, Shoes &amp; Slippers Flour and Oatmeal Coffins Drapery Brooms and Brushes Wines and Spirits Leather, &amp; 'Shoemakers' Beer and Stout Necessaries *Men's Suits Tailors' Goods *lronmongery ; Butter, Bacon, Cheese, Drugs. Lard, Margarine. *Dressings Cutlery Soda Water Tobacco and Snuff Paints, &amp;c. ' Fish and Ice *Electrical Goods. , Butchers' Meat *Kitchen Utensils. *NO GOODS OF GERMAN OR AUSTRIAN ORIGIN WILL BE ACCEPTED. Separate tenders must be sent for the Work- house and Cottage Homes, and samples of the articles required can be seen at either institu- tion between the hours of 10 a.m. and 4 p.m. The fuel to he supplied must be accord- ing to the specification as set forth on the tender form, and quotations must be made for delivery, either to the new siding adjoining the Workhouse, or by cart, and by cart to the Cot- tage• Homes. • Forms of tender, and instructions to persons tendering (which must be strictly complied with), may be obtained from the undersigned. All accounts will be paid monthly.. The Guardians do not necessarily bind them- selves to accept the lowest or any tender. By order, ARTHUR B orrom LEY. Clerk to the Guardians. Bew,:er Chambers. Warrington, 111 Alarelt. 1916.</p>
